description:
FILED s530b (Opus agent, 2026-10-31), from the Template-Toolkit re-census.  PRE-EXISTING.  SILENT (the output goes nowhere).

    my $r = "";
    open(Foo::OUT, ">", \$r) or die;
    eval "package Foo; print OUT qq{a}; 1" or print "ERR $@";
    package Foo; print OUT "b";
    package main; close Foo::OUT;
    print "[$r]\n";
perl: [ab].  PCL: [b] -- the file-level `package Foo; print OUT` is right, the same statement in a STRING EVAL after `package Foo;` is not.  The tied-handle spelling (TIEHANDLE on *Foo::OUT, `print OUT` / `printf OUT` in the eval) loses both too: scratch/s530b/p/tieh.pl, perl [a 007 b c], PCL [b c].
Probably the eval-mode name resolution of a bareword handle (the #240 family: the region package `p-eval-thunk` binds) -- the handle's NAME is resolved against main, not the eval's current package.

Template-Toolkit: Template::Directive::perl generates `tie *Template::Perl::PERLOUT, 'Template::TieString', \$_tt_result; ... eval "package Template::Perl; ... print PERLOUT ..."` -- t/evalperl.t rows 17 and 23 (`print PERLOUT "\nbar\n"`, `printf PERLOUT "value: %05d\n", 7` lost).
